{"kind":"assert","text":"Cutover head (05d618e2): question 10, and more format changes. The source pass over replay, client, mcp, git, contract, cli and the apps is committed. Source outside tests now reads inc only in the held stand-ins of question 9 and in two generated files that need a rebuild.\n\nQuestion 10. OriginalRow.to is a ScopeRef, and a ScopeRef no longer carries a kind. The room page uses row.to.kind === \"directory\" to aim an opening act at the directory's current partition. This happens at apps/room/page/src/open-requests.ts:25 and 38, and at original-check.ts:72 and 141. What replaces that kind?\n(a) The original-copy row records the kind, or the definition, of its target.\n(b) The page compares row.to.scope with the room's known directory and partition scope IDs.\n(c) The client originals record carries the intent's sourceKind.\nI recommend (b). The page already holds those IDs, and the check stays true to the rule that a sender-written kind proves nothing. The four sites are unchanged until you answer.\n\nFormat changes in addition to da1a7606:\n- the scope-index manifest rows become { at: { scope, genesis }, kind }, with no separate genesis field;\n- the journal parent binding records [\"scope\", \"genesis\"];\n- the git attempt storage key uses genesis;\n- the MCP views scope schema is { scope, genesis };\n- the room page's list-context and room-context storage keys use genesis;\n- visible text says genesis where it said incarnation: archived, accepted, coverage and author lines.\n\nAlso: command-verify's sessionDeniedDependency now asks that the missing fact be a genesis (seq 0 and hash equal to at.genesis). The match against the register's results stands in for the old directory-kind check."}